1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,520
In this video we'll look at using SAML to configure user groups and permissions.

2
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:16,680
You can also combine SAML with SCIM, enabling you to use SAML for authentication and SCIM

3
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:20,160
to manage users and user groups.

4
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:24,640
This provides you with greater transparency because it allows you to view key details

5
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:29,320
about your users and groups from Burp Suite Enterprise.

6
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:35,080
Before you can use SAML to configure user groups, you first need to set up an LDAP or SAML connection

7
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:38,480
for single sign-on.

8
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:42,520
If you would like to create groups using SAML without SCIM integration, you will first need

9
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:47,740
to log in to Burp Suite Enterprise as an administrator.

10
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:52,180
From the team menu, select groups.

11
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:57,020
Create a new group representing each of the groups of users in your LDAP or SAML identity

12
00:00:57,020 --> 00:00:59,200
provider.

13
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:03,520
Make sure the groups have the same names as the ones you sent from Active Directory or

14
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:06,680
your SAML identity provider.

15
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:13,580
If you manage your users directly in Azure Active Directory, you will need to use the group ID.

16
00:01:13,580 --> 00:01:19,760
You can find more on this in our section on Configuring SAML SSO with Azure Directory.

17
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:21,680
Assign roles to your groups as required.

18
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:25,660
If you don't assign any roles although your users would be able to log in, they wouldn't

19
00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:29,320
be able to access any functionality.

20
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:34,200
You can also limit which sites users in a particular group can access by applying site restrictions

21
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:36,800
for each group.

22
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:41,120
You can also limit which sites users in a particular group.

23
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:44,280
Save your changes and you're all done.

